# The signed approvals, part `front-ends`: the password asked for at a
# terminal and in the application, and what it signs. Written with the code.

# ------------------------------------------------ the guards

[break] a-sessions-command-may-reset-the-password
rule: Guard A: the permission engine, given the command line's own grammar, refuses `cineris approvals reset` to every command of a session; `approvals status` only reads.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/nested.rs
in: standing
find: ApprovalsCommand::Reset => approves("approvals reset")
replace: ApprovalsCommand::Reset => Standing::Safe
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris nested::tests::each_command_is_refused_by_the_engine_exactly_when_its_standing_says
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris nested::tests::the_engines_table_reads_the_same_with_this_grammar

[break] the-fallback-lets-the-password-be-reset
rule: Guard A without a front end's grammar: the engine's fallback refuses `cineris approvals reset` as it refuses `approvals setup`.
file: crates/cineris-policy/src/approving.rs
find: ("approvals", Some(&["setup", "reset"]))
replace: ("approvals", Some(&["setup"]))
caught-by:
    cineris-policy approving::tests::the_fallback_refuses_exactly_the_tables_refused_lines

[break] reset-runs-under-a-sessions-command
rule: Guard B: `cineris approvals reset` refuses under a session's command, before it reads anything.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/approvals.rs
in: approvals
find: crate::not_under_a_session(name, "approvals reset")
replace: Ok::<(), u8>(())
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system nested::sys_cineris_run_by_a_sessions_command_is_held_or_refused

# ------------------------------------------------ at a terminal

[break] a-hash-approves-with-no-terminal
rule: With no terminal there is no signed approval: `--hash` checks what is shown, and approves nothing on its own.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/ext.rs
in: signing
find: _ => Signing::NoTerminal
replace: _ => Signing::Ask
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris ext::tests::a_signed_change_is_asked_only_at_a_terminal_and_no_hash_replaces_it

[break] a-headless-run-at-a-terminal-does-not-open-the-approvals
rule: A headless run at a terminal that has approvals to use opens them with the key the typed password makes, before its session opens.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/approvals.rs
in: open_at_start
find: .open_approvals(&key)
replace: .approval_key().map(|_| ())
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::system approvals::sys_a_headless_run_with_no_terminal_asks_nothing_and_says_why

# ------------------------------------------------ in the application

[break] the-session-opens-before-the-password
rule: When a session has approvals to use, the application holds its open until the password is answered: the approvals open first.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/app/state/approvals.rs
in: App::approvals_hold
find: Some(here) if here.holding => {
replace: Some(here) if here.holding && here.held.is_some() => {
caught-by:
    cineris-tui app::state::approvals::tests::a_session_with_approvals_to_use_opens_after_the_password

[break] the-trust-questions-yes-goes-unsigned
rule: A yes to a trust question that proposes what it writes is answered only with the person's signature, made from the password the dialog asked for.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::answer
find: && request.proposal.is_some()
replace: && request.proposal.is_none()
caught-by:
    cineris-tui app::state::approvals::tests::the_trust_questions_yes_signs_with_the_password_and_nothing_else_holds_it
    cineris-tui app::state::approvals::tests::a_wrong_password_at_the_yes_asks_again_and_esc_is_not_now

[break] the-terminal-stays-open-while-the-application-asks
rule: While the application asks for the password, the terminal is closed to other programs (its exclusive mode), and open again once the dialog has gone.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/app.rs
in: draw
find: let _ = terminal.set_exclusive(app.asking_password());
replace:
caught-by:
    cineris-tui app::tests::the_loop_closes_the_terminal_to_others_while_the_password_is_asked

[break] a-paste-the-loop-reads-is-left-unwiped
rule: Each paste the application's loop reads is written over once it is done with.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/app.rs
in: forget
find: crate::secret::password::forget(event);
replace: drop(event);
caught-by:
    cineris-tui app::tests::the_loop_writes_over_each_paste_it_reads

[break] a-paste-the-prompt-takes-is-left-unwiped
rule: Each paste the password's prompt reads at a terminal is written over once it is done with.
file: crates/cineris-tui/src/secret/password.rs
in: ask_on
find: forget(event);
replace: drop(event);
caught-by:
    cineris-tui secret::password::tests::at_a_terminal_each_paste_is_written_over_once_read

[break] the-exclusive-mode-is-lost-across-a-stop
rule: On Unix the terminal's exclusive mode, turned off when the program is stopped, is on again when it is continued.
file: crates/cineris-term/src/sys/unix.rs
in: on_stop
find: exclusive_mode(true);
replace:
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-term::it exclusive::sys_the_exclusive_mode_holds_and_comes_back_after_a_stop
